      "writtenOn": "2026-08-12T18:03:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is unfortunate. I wonder if we could switch the CpuBuffer implementations to use a copy-on-write model so that when we record the draw here, we just get a new SkMesh that takes a ref on the same SkData objects.\n\nThat wouldn\u0027t have to be in this CL, but I think we should file a new bug to track additional improvements to make drawMesh work better in Graphite\u0027s model. This also applies to the virtuals on IndexBuffer and VertexBuffer. It would be good to support a Graphite-backed implementation that owned its own Buffer objects. At that point, we could use the direct draw functions on DrawWriter like you used with the appended CPU data. However, we would need a new update function that either took a recorder or a context to control how the operations were ordered on the GPU timeline.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 991,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1006,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "5614afbee782fbc27db274b81b02512562f5474f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "44cc839d_9c240165",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/Device.cpp",
