      "message": "I don\u0027t think it\u0027s necessary to have a separate MeshSpecificationDictionary type. We should be able to have `set` be overloaded based on the type, and then we just need to have two versions of `find`. \n\nIf you prefer to keep MeshSpecificationDictionary separate, we don\u0027t need to wrap it in an `sk_sp` here. Its lifetime ought to be tied exactly with the `RuntimeEffectDictionary` so could just be a direct field.",
