      "message": "We don\u0027t get the varying size from the spec, only the gpu type of varyings. Although I don\u0027t think it would be necessary to hash on size for varyings since even if we get a collision and use an existing mesh shader snippet even though its not the correct one for the current specification. The resulting SkSL for the vertex and fragment shader which defines the varyings would still be valid since it would be reliant only on the mesh specification referenced by that existing shader snippet id, and varyings are not written from CPU data like attributes and uniforms are.",
